## Application testing from natural-language instructions

Agent QA runs web, Android, and iOS application tests described in natural language. It stores execution memory for reuse and can recover when a previously observed UI path changes. A CLI and dashboard support test authoring, execution, and inspection of run artifacts.

The MCP server and Agent Skills expose testing workflows to compatible coding assistants. The full MCP authoring, execution, and triage workflow connects to a running Agent QA dashboard API.

## Setup and cost

The CLI requires Node.js 24 or newer and installs with `npm install -D agent-qa`. Test execution requires a configured model provider and a browser or mobile device environment; Android and iOS testing use Appium.

The software has no fee for uses permitted by its source-available FSL-1.1-ALv2 license. Model, browser, and device provider costs are separate. The Free pricing tag refers to the software, not bundled provider credits.

See the [quickstart](https://vostride.com/docs/agent-qa/quickstart) for setup and the [source license](https://github.com/vostride/agent-qa/blob/main/LICENSE.md) for permitted uses.
